  "scope": "Same shared separate-object rig with every previous runtime/art byte and all seventeen prior profiles preserved, including EXP050. Uses only accepted bilateral ordinary-lid, uneven rigid brow, sealed smile/spread, independent positive corner and sealed-width values. No opening, forced closed smile-eye contour, purse, pressure, oral lift, inner-brow lift, gaze, blush, hair, head or body movement. Canonical lower-lid curve and lip fullness remain disclosed approximations. No new shape, control, range, pigment or source-UV change.",
  "interpolation": "The quiet initial tenth of a second acknowledges KP1/2 before a compact, purposeful onset. Bilateral amused narrowing and the broad biased sealed grin gather together into the stronger peak by 1.02 seconds. A 0.45-second peak hold gives the smug watching gaze time to read. The exact eased peak arrives at 1.74 seconds and holds for 0.28 seconds; it is the same family with the accepted small eye reopening, not a new smile. Recovery reaches the exact KP7 anchor at 2.58 seconds, with more open eyes and a smaller lingering grin. Exact neutral starts at 3.18 seconds and remains for 0.22 seconds. This is newly authored timing, not recovered source motion. It does not reuse EXP102's slow smirk build or EXP181's unilateral wink accent. The unchanged shared cubic smoothstep joins exact accepted anchors and duplicate hold keys. Initial trigger blending lasts 0.30 seconds and therefore attenuates only the early onset, not any nonzero source anchor. Existing release remains 0.45 seconds. Natural playback stays sealed; width is never combined with positive opening. No new control value or pose refinement is introduced.",
